  "id": "Compound::DB08899 - Gene::1558",
  "verbalization": "Enzalutamide is shown to bind to Cyp2b6, which is involved in the metabolic pathways of diclofenac and arachidonic acid. This binding suggests a potential role in modulating the activity of Cyp2c8, as Cyp2b6 is functionally linked to Cyp2c8 through participation in metabolic processes. The evidence from the three paths indicates that Enzalutamide may influence Cyp2c8 through a mechanism involving Cyp2b6, which is part of a broader metabolic network. The shared involvement of Cyp2b6 in multiple metabolic pathways supports the idea that Enzalutamide could affect Cyp2c8 by altering the activity of its interacting enzymes. The final scores suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, but further experimental validation would be necessary to confirm the direct impact of Enzalutamide on Cyp2c8.",
